"""Baseline Suitability Model for Protected Area Prediction (Random Forest)

Purpose: Estimate how "protection-like" each pixel looked in year 2000.
         A model trained only on 2000 (protected vs unprotected) learns the
         spatial signature of protected areas. Its predicted probability for
         each unprotected pixel becomes a suitability score. We then check
         whether high-suitability pixels actually became protected by 2024.

Features:
- Leakage prevention: exclude denylist matches and target (is_protected_2000); hard-fail
  only if any excluded column survives in final feature list; excluded_cols and
  final_feature_cols logged and in metrics; leakage audit (top correlations with target).
- Splits: random split + spatial blocked train/test (val held out, not used for model selection).
- Future status: DuckDB parquet aggregation (threads from SLURM/cpu_count); pandas fallback
  if DuckDB missing; backend and duckdb/matplotlib availability recorded in metrics.
- Tie handling: deterministic precision@k under ties; tie diagnostics for suitability.
- Thesis artifacts: metrics JSON, LaTeX table, PR/ROC plots, suitability map (Easting/Northing axes);
  dataset/schema hashes and config snapshot in metrics.

Input:   `merged_panel_final.parquet` (same locations as model1_preprocessing)
Output:  - Trained Random Forest model (baseline_rf_2000.pkl)
         - Suitability scores (baseline_scores_2000_rf.parquet)
         - Evaluation metrics (baseline_rf_metrics.json)
         - LaTeX table, PR/ROC plots, suitability map (outputs/south_america/results/ml_baselines)
         - Scored outcome table (baseline_scored_outcomes_rf.parquet)
"""

